%%{init: {'fontFamily':'Inter, Helvetica, Arial, sans-serif'}}%%
sequenceDiagram
    autonumber
    actor Op as Operator
    participant W as Worker wrap-up
    participant S as Storage
    participant A as Adapter module
    participant B as Backend
    participant Q as VconQueue
    participant R as Redis
    participant API as API

    Note over W,R: Write path after the last link
    W->>R: RPUSH to each egress list, before any storage write
    loop Each backend, threads when CONSERVER_PARALLEL_STORAGE is on and there are two or more
        W->>S: Storage(name).save(vcon_id)
        S->>A: module.save(vcon_id, options)
        A->>R: VconRedis.get_vcon(vcon_id)
        R-->>A: vCon body
        A->>B: write
        alt Write succeeds
            A-->>W: returns, conserver.storage.count outcome=success
        else Adapter raises
            A-->>W: exception, outcome=error
            W->>Q: enqueue_storage_dlq(name, vcon_id, VCON_DLQ_EXPIRY)
            Q->>R: EVAL, one atomic script
            alt Body exists
                Note over R: Raise a shorter TTL to the retention value, then RPUSH DLQ:storage:#lt;name#gt;
                R-->>Q: list length
                Q-->>W: conserver.dlq.count incremented
            else Body missing
                R-->>Q: -1
                Q-->>W: ValueError
                Note over W: Logged as manual recovery required, never re-raised
            end
        end
    end
    Note over W: A failed backend does not stop the other backends or re-run the chain

    Note over Op,API: Recovery path, driven by the operator
    Op->>API: GET /dlq/storage?storage_name=#lt;name#gt;
    API->>R: LRANGE 0 -1
    R-->>API: pending vCon ids
    API-->>Op: JSON list of ids
    Op->>API: POST /dlq/storage/reprocess?storage_name=#lt;name#gt;#amp;count=N
    alt Backend not configured or adapter fails to load
        API-->>Op: 404
    else Replay lock is already held
        API->>R: acquire DLQ:storage:#lt;name#gt;:replay-lock, non-blocking, no expiry
        API-->>Op: 409
    else Lock acquired
        API->>R: LRANGE 0 count-1, a snapshot that removes nothing
        loop Each id in the snapshot
            API->>S: save(vcon_id) in the threadpool
            S->>A: module.save(vcon_id, options)
            A->>R: VconRedis.get_vcon(vcon_id)
            A->>B: write
            alt Write succeeds
                API->>R: LREM one entry
            else Adapter raises
                Note over API: Warning logged, entry stays, batch stops
            end
        end
        API->>R: release the lock
        API-->>Op: 200 with the number written
    end
